    "abstract": "This report summarises the findings of the Marine Spatial Planning Addressing Climate Effects project (MSPACE, 2021-2026) in Welsh marine waters (Wales, UK). It includes key findings from novel research into: 1) the potential effects of climate change in this region of UK marine waters; 2) the structure of the region's blue economy; and 3) knowledge co-creation activities with marine stakeholders in the region. Through these activities, we draw up key recommendations for climate-resilient, economically sensible and socially acceptable strategies to manage marine space trough the Welsh National Marine Plan, leading to climate change adaptation and mitigation.",
    "field": "Climate-smart marine spatial planning",
    "problem": "Current marine spatial planning inadequately addresses climate change, threatening the effectiveness of conservation efforts and the viability of marine industries in Welsh waters, which necessitates the development of economically and socially acceptable climate-smart management plans.",
    "method": "The paper proposes co-creating alternative spatial management scenarios with stakeholders, evaluating them against environmental and socio-economic metrics, and using multi-criteria decision analysis to identify socially acceptable options for climate-smart marine planning.",
    "task": "The task is to co-create and evaluate alternative climate-smart marine spatial management scenarios for Welsh waters, assessing their environmental, economic, and social outcomes to support climate change adaptation and mitigation planning.",
